  "penalties": [],
  "extra_findings": [
    "F2, listing and CSV parts (the finding is credited once, to SEC-017): listarChamados (index.php:73) and exportarCsv (index.php:45) gave every ticket to any logged-in client. The delivery now passes an owner filter for non-technicians, while technicians and two-argument callers still get every ticket. That is enforcement, not COMP (as for O).",
    "F5, apart from the fp leak: every export rewrote the fixed EXPORT_DIR/chamados.csv and read it back (lib.php:125-150). Concurrent exports could mix, a file holding every ticket stayed on disk, and a failed fopen produced an empty response. The CSV is now streamed to php://output, which is not COMP (as for K).",
    "F7, second part: mediaResposta loaded every answered row to average it in PHP (lib.php:109-116). It now uses AVG() in SQL.",
    "F8, apart from fixation: the session cookie had no httponly, samesite or strict mode, and an array-valued login, senha or busca raised a TypeError (HTTP 500). Fixed with session_start options and is_string checks (delivered index.php:15-19, 25-26, 80).",
    "F10: no limit on login attempts (index.php:20-29). Not fixed.",
    "F12, other parts: formatarStatus returns 'Resolvido' for any status other than 1 and 2 (lib.php:26-35). That is contracted legacy behaviour, kept unchanged, so it is an extra with no COMP (rule 14). The finding also makes a generic remark that error handling and logging are missing.",
    "Non-changes list: the login form has no CSRF token and there is no logout or security headers. SEC-005 is a legitimate flaw outside the matrix (matrix note)."
  ],
